        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Put "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "landscapes",
            "ref": "v-landscape"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " into your "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "suitcase",
            "ref": "v-suitcase"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and bring them home. That idea sounds nice but a little crazy, doesn’t it? In fact, Kathleen Vance has been doing just that."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Vance is not a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "magician",
            "ref": "v-magician"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "; she is an artist. She is famous for creating "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "miniature",
            "ref": "v-miniature"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " landscapes inside old suitcases. All her pieces use real soil, grass, plants and water. These works are living and breathing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Vance grew up on a farm in Maryland. She lived in New York City after graduating from university. In that big city, she often wanted to get close to nature. She also hoped to bring nature into people’s everyday lives. And so the “Travelling Landscapes” series was born."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "By putting nature into boxes, the artist shows that the environment "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "belongs to",
            "ref": "v-belong-to"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " each one of us. “I want people to enjoy nature and think about how they would "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "personally",
            "ref": "v-personally"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " be able to protect it. We all exist on the Earth, and some people are lucky enough to own parts of the land. How they take care of it is something they should consider,” she explained."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
